 # License
 
 Project released under MIT license. More license information can be found in assets folder. 
+
+
+## Full keyboard and optional text-entry example
+
+The Linux adapter recognizes the official CardputerZero symbol codes, ordinary
+letters/numbers, Shift, Fn editing controls and Help/PrintScreen. Built-in and US
+USB keyboard profiles are separate; it does not assume every keyboard uses a US
+layout. Use the shared cp0 SDK backend instead if that is already your input path;
+do not decode its translated characters a second time.
+
+A focused LVGL textarea selects text context automatically. An application can
+supply `platform::set_text_entry_query()` for a custom editor/focus model; clear
+the query when its owner is destroyed. Outside text entry, existing navigation
+shortcuts remain available. Printable toolbar shortcuts cannot consume typed
+numbers/letters, while Help/PrintScreen are routed before the focused editor.
+
+For the optional counter-page editor, configure with `-DAPP_KEYBOARD_EXAMPLE=ON`,
+build normally and open the second page. Type ordinary letters/numbers and all
+printed Sym combinations, including Sym+N `/`, then exercise Shift, Fn arrows,
+Home/End/Delete, Help, Tab and Escape. The example is off by default, keeps text
+only in RAM and adds no hardware service. It is not a complete notes application.
+
+`BUILD_TESTING=ON` adds portable decoder checks; on Linux it also compiles the
+actual evdev reader against synthetic pipe records and a real LVGL textarea.
+Run `ctest --test-dir <build-dir> --output-on-failure`. The independent original
+32-entry fixture is not generated from the decoder. Tests cover context changes
+within a batch, shortcut consumption, rollover, event loss, disconnect and bounded
+polling. They do not open input devices, inject kernel events or qualify physical
+keys, firmware one-shot/lock behavior or the entire default application's UI.
+
+See [keyboard attribution](NOTICE.keyboard.md) and the fixture provenance before
+reusing these MIT components. This proposal is based on a pinned Template revision;
+upstream changes must be reviewed before rebasing it.
